  TUL SPAN DECODER ON: layers=2 heads=8 J=32x1 offset=1 weight=1.0 — span s+1 is decoded from z with a teacher-forced token path (morph/model/tul_spandec.py)
  TUL THOUGHT REGISTER ON: slot_cells=4 init='distinct' - each span gets M MUTABLE looped cells instead of one, seeded apart by M learned queries pooling the span's own prelude states (W_o zero-init: step 0 IS the ruler). They loop together at one per-slot depth; inside the loop a cell reads every cell of earlier slots AND every cell of its own slot, LATER siblings included (the relation travels as `tg_relation` and REPLACES the attention branches' causal term; through `tg_allow` it would only narrow and would execute as plain flattened causal - measured and fixed 2026-09-13). The M cells are LXTUL's K streams and every one of them is written 1:1 into ITS prefix cell (fan_mix=all; see the LXTUL FAN line below). the coda is unchanged, and the span decoder grades the MEAN of the M cells. Built against the measured rank collapse (slot_eff_rank 5.7-7.3 in 1024 dims, pairwise cos 0.72-0.77). Read `val/slot_cell_eff_rank` - the rank WITHIN a slot - beside `val/slot_eff_rank` (lab/experiments/planned/2026-09-13-arc-thought-register.md)
  LXTUL FAN ON: fan_k=4 mix='all' repel_mode='epivol' repel_lambda=0.1 repel_passes=2 prefix_k=4 ALL eps=0.05 wta_lambda=0.0 (no mixture, no gate: every stream is written into ITS prefix cell through W_prefix[i], the register's 1:1 route, and the coda reads all K; wta_lambda 0: NO responsibility term and NO extra coda pass) LATENT-SELECTED LOOP 'joint': after every pass the M cells of a continuing slot are reset to the winner (train: follow the ROUTER; the teacher is the argmin ||g(cell) - z||^2 on the EMA-prelude target, EMA m=0.996; eval and slots without a target: the router, rank 64, CE onto the teacher at weight 1.0); ONE latent loss at the exit (relaxed WTA eps=0.05, weight 1.0, head reads DETACHED cells: ranks only, no pull on the loop; online floor 0.2 @ 0.1); the coda reads the final winner alone (the coda's CE reaches the loop through the winner) - read fan/lsel_r2, fan/lsel_teacher_router_agree (chance 1/K), fan/lsel_switch_rate, fan/lsel_cell_spread, and at val fan/lsel_teacher_pick_gap - K latent STREAMS per span through the ONE shared core. The streams ARE the Thought Register's cells (fan_k aliases slot_cells, so the message above is this arm's loop); what is NEW is the three things the register did not have. (1) a DIVERSITY term ('epivol') charged after passes 1..2 only, because PLR Thm 4.4 makes the collapse exponential in depth (pass 1 fights L^2, pass 6 fights L^12). (2) the exit WRITE: every stream in its own prefix cell, the register's 1:1 route, so the coda's width is prefix_k=4 and the width partner is the ruler at the same prefix_k. (3) the ORACLE: at every val the coda is re-run once per stream and `fan/oracle_ce` is the per-span minimum. READ `fan/oracle_ce` AGAINST `fan/single_ce` FIRST - if the gap is inside a width control's own CE gain, the streams are copies and the width branch closes, whatever `fan/mixed_ce` says. Then `fan/stream_cos_t{t}` (1.0 = collapsed; the register read 0.94) and `fan/stream_rank_t{t}` (the register read 1.24 of 4) (lab/experiments/planned/2026-09-19-lxtul-fan4.md)
  TUL TG-RESTRICT ON: soft_prev_span=False — window branch restricted to same-span-or-slot, compressed branch restricted to slot positions (docs/tul-tg-spec.md); model.use_kernels must be false
  TUL STRICT GEOMETRY ON (coda_prefix_reach=all): the prelude is same-span ONLY, a coda prefix cell reads itself alone, the conv/value-shift and the retention carry reset at every segment, and the coda's per-layer injections at the slot cells are zeroed — the slot LOOP is the only cross-span channel (lab/experiments/planned/2026-09-12-arc-strict-geometry.md)
  TUL SLOT-CELL PASS NORM 'rms' ON: after EVERY slot-loop pass each carried cell is RMSNorm(h) * g (per Hyper-Connection stream over the channels, eps 1e-6, ONE learned gain g shared by every pass, init 1.0, no-decay, never ternary); the entry state is NOT normed. The fixed-point term compares normed states; the latent head, the teacher, the diversity term and the prefix write read the normed cell. NOTE the gain hinge (model.slot_gain_lambda=100.0) still reads the RAW map f, not the normed map the loop carries: it bounds f, not the carried gain - read val/slot_cell_rms_t{t} (should sit at rms(g)) and val/slot_cell_norm_g_mean / _std
  TG SCOPED KERNELS ON: HC-Cayley + CCA prologue + core window fused; TG-restricted attention branches eager by construction; CE chunked
  TUL POINTER ON: 4 heads over earlier tokens' final hidden states (token order, j < i), each read as a distribution over the token that followed j, gated with the model's head; output-only; 529,673 params, never ternary; cell keys off; coverage lambda 0.0
